{"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Tries\/Se","doc:\/\/Tries\/SE","doc:\/\/Tries\/SQ","doc:\/\/Tries\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/Tries\/SH","doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Tries\/ST","doc:\/\/Tries\/s10SetAlgebraP"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It holds the same keys and answers the same queries as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", with the same names, but has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a vertex per key and per branching point rather than per symbol: O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") vertices for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keys,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"however long they are. That suits keys with long shared prefixes, such as file paths or URLs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Lookup, insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"d"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols that passes "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"d","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" vertices of at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children."}]},{"code":["let paths = RadixTree([\"\/usr\/bin\", \"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"])","paths.contains(\"\/usr\/lib\")                                   \/\/ true","paths.elements(withPrefix: \"\/usr\/l\").map { String($0) }      \/\/ [\"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"]","paths.longestPrefix(of: \"\/usr\/bin\/swift\").map { String($0) } \/\/ \"\/usr\/bin\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"text":" links, and the edge labels are slices of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer of symbols, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 vertices and label symbols, and copying","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/PrefixView"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/count","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/isEmpty"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/contains(_:)-39nls","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/elements(withPrefix:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/hasPrefix(_:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/insert(_:)-3ywij","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/longestPrefix(of:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/remove(_:)-3svqg"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/Tries\